# [PANRG](../wg/panrg.html)

## Summary

The Path-Aware Networking Research Group (PANRG) met at IETF 127. The session was chaired by Jen Linkova (with Brian Trammell absent due to travel). The agenda featured two technical presentations followed by Q&A and group discussion:
1. An exploration of protocol-agnostic in-network retransmissions for encrypted transport protocols (PAC RAT).
2. A proposal for adapting Happy Eyeballs to path-aware networks, specifically targeting SCION path selection.

